{"name":"Coral Tree","hex":"#ab6e67","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coral tree","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the trees of the genus Erythrina, of most tropical and subtropical regions."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coral_tree"}],"entries":[{"title":"Erythrina","blocks":[{"text":"Erythrina is a genus of plants in the pea family, Fabaceae. It contains about 130 species, which are distributed in tropical and subtropical regions worldwide. They are trees, with the larger species growing up to 30 m (98 ft) in height. These species are known for their large flowers with long and bright red or orange petals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Starr_050721-7264_Erythrina_sandwicensis.jpg/330px-Starr_050721-7264_Erythrina_sandwicensis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erythrina","wikidata":"Q1340386"},{"title":"Coral","blocks":[{"text":"Corals are colonial marine invertebrates within the subphylum Anthozoa of the phylum Cnidaria. They typically form compact colonies of many identical individual polyps. Coral species include the important reef builders that inhabit tropical oceans and secrete calcium carbonate to form a hard skeleton."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Coral_Outcrop_Flynn_Reef.jpg/330px-Coral_Outcrop_Flynn_Reef.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral","wikidata":"Q171446"},{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usages, the definition of a tree may be narrower, e.g., including only woody plants with secondary growth, only plants that are usable for timber, or only plants above a specified height. Wider definitions include taller palms, tree ferns, bananas, and bamboos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree","wikidata":"Q10884"},{"title":"Coral (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The various tones of the color coral are orange, red and pink representations of the colors of those cnidarians known as precious corals."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral_(color)","wikidata":"Q2411228"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Erythrina_flabelliformis_MHNT.BOT.2009.13.50.jpg/500px-Erythrina_flabelliformis_MHNT.BOT.2009.13.50.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Erythrina_flabelliformis_MHNT.BOT.2009.13.50.jpg/1280px-Erythrina_flabelliformis_MHNT.BOT.2009.13.50.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Erythrina_flabelliformis_MHNT.BOT.2009.13.50.jpg/500px-Erythrina_flabelliformis_MHNT.BOT.2009.13.50.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Erythrina flabelliformis - MHNT","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AErythrina_flabelliformis_MHNT.BOT.2009.13.50.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Asian_Pied_Starling_%28Sturnus_contra%29_feeding_on_Indian_Coral_Tree_%28Erythrina_variegata%29_in_Kolkata_I_IMG_4005.jpg/330px-Asian_Pied_Starling_%28Sturnus_contra%29_feeding_on_Indian_Coral_Tree_%28Erythrina_variegata%29_in_Kolkata_I_IMG_4005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Asian_Pied_Starling_%28Sturnus_contra%29_feeding_on_Indian_Coral_Tree_%28Erythrina_variegata%29_in_Kolkata